    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d356-a3">

                <pb facs="0830" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg782"/>

                <head ana="#head_untitled-missing-head-in-printed-volume">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Yokohama,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 25, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Information having been received by me that
                    the consuls of Italy and Prussia are authorized to make known to the subjects of
                    those powers that they can proceed to Ne-egata after the 15th July next, for the
                    purpose of carrying on such trade as is permitted by the treaties, I deem it my
                    duty to inform you that the Japanese ministers for foreign affairs have
                    communicated to me the fact that a state of war is existing at Ne-egata, and
                    therefore I deem it unavoidable at this moment to declare that port opened to
                    American citizens.</p>
                <p>As soon, however, as it is deemed safe for the purpose of trade I shall give you
                    further information.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, sir, very respectfully, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>R. B. VAN VALKENBURGH.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>General J. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stahel</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >United States Consul, Kanagawa.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
